{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017PuDcTfrZmfnUAqxba4h8S","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-10-14 03:00 +07\n2\t# Task: plan phase 8, the cutover (Architect; plan only, no code, no docs)\n3\tYou are claude-fable-5-1, NEW session. Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8plan` (branch `srvm-phase8-plan` = the integration branch `srvm-phase7`: phases 1-7 complete, lanes running; it lands on master first). Edit ONLY your report `collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md`. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3 (cursor, cursor cell, cursor-ref, cell).\n4\tPhase 8 per `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` section 10 item 8 (\"Cutover\"): delete `yin.vm.semantic` (old); rename `yin.vm.semantic-register` to `yin.vm.semantic`; remove the old H/R request paths and the `raise` dependency; remove the `:dim/lift-to` row from both de Bruijn descriptors without a version bump and regenerate the descriptor hashes and every pinned H and R (derivations design 8.1-8.2); delete `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve`, `yin.vm.debruijn-linearize`, `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile` and their tests only after the replacement coverage of continuation 8.4 is green and the descriptor-hash golden has moved to a surviving namespace; switch `linker/relowered`, `publish-closure!` and the REPL to the A-derived lowerings (derivations design 8.3); regenerate the manifests' derivation records as `A -> H`, `A -> R` and the format index `{format storage-address}` (derivations 7.6, 8.1); run the C4 suite over the newly published images as the install-child gate (derivations 6.1.4 (c)); finalize documentation; no compatibility shim.\n5\tOwner rulings that bind (2026-10-10..14): A is the only code identity; R and H are derived checksums from A; BLAKE3 everywhere (the H and R checksums, descriptor hashes, and the old de Bruijn hashes that SURVIVE move from SHA-256 to BLAKE3 at this cutover; dao.jing keeps SHA-256 as an explicitly mintable registry member); the AST is never lost; no backward compatibility (regenerate, never migrate); `debruijn/stack.cljc` and `debruijn/register.cljc` are BACKENDS of the semantic-register VM, kept after phase 8, documented fragment, not widened (so they are NOT deleted); the old codec versions 0/1/2 and the old inspector/handoff leave at phase 8 along with the old semantic VM that produced them (verify what depends on them: `handoff.cljc`, `checkpoint.cljc`, `lift_support`, old tests); the REPL custody gap (the REPL composes the old kernel) closes here by the rename; the other orchestrator (yang.python/C4, do NOT touch their worktrees `datomworld-c4-*` or uncommitted edits; notes via collab/ relayed by the owner) has the C4 track whose scanners and pinned A addresses regenerate at the cutover; implementation goes to CODEX, reviews to Fable/opus; tests: quick tier at every landing, slow tier before big merges and at phase boundaries, three hosts, servers shiva/jupiter (docs/agents/build-n-test.md).\n6\tDo: (1) an INVENTORY with file:line of everything the cutover touches: namespaces to delete (with their tests and what each test pins), namespaces to rename (every require site across src/ test/ docs/ scripts: count), every pinned H, R, descriptor hash and A address (goldens, fixtures, scanner goldens, manifests, `ucf` fixtures including the ones 7a regenerated), the old transport paths (version 0/1/2 codec, `handoff.cljc` export-task/resume-task, old inspector `checkpoint.cljc`, `lift_support` legacy paths, old harness) and which tests still exercise them (to delete or keep), and the SHA-256 sites that move to BLAKE3 (use `grep` over src/test; the old `yin.vm.debruijn` dimension/node hashes: say which namespaces survive and so which hashes move vs die, with evidence: who requires them); the `encode-scalar` hazard (`debruijn_register_code` calls `debruijn-code/encode-scalar`); the REPL and `publish-closure!`/`linker/relowered` switch points. (2) The DESIGN QUESTIONS phase 8 forces, each with a recommendation and cost, flagging which the OWNER must decide (e.g. whether the old handoff/codec versions die now, the rename mechanics for a namespace that other tracks and docs cite, what happens to the old harness and stage tests of the old kernel, regeneration of the C4 goldens and who does it, any irreversible deletion order). (3) A SLICING: slices 8a, 8b, ... each with files, dependencies, acceptance (named tests), hosts, and a day estimate for codex implementation plus Fable/opus review rounds (we average 2-4 review rounds per slice), ordering and what can run concurrently, and the gate list: quick tier per slice, slow tier at the end, C4 suite, three hosts. (4) Risks (mass rename conflicts with the other orchestrator's branches; accidental loss of coverage when deleting tests; hash regeneration drift; Dart cljd name resolution on rename) and mitigations; the rollback story. (5) An honest total estimate. Foreground only. Report starts with a 15-line plain summary for the owner and ends READY or NOT READY (with the blocking owner questions).\n7\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14576d0d-3405-4311-bbba-ad13d850656b","uuid":"75b45936-bfc3-4697-bb1e-b7280b3d6dd5","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:02:54.695Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8plan/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.prompt.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 03:00 +07\n# Task: plan phase 8, the cutover (Architect; plan only, no code, no docs)\nYou are claude-fable-5-1, NEW session. Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8plan` (branch `srvm-phase8-plan` = the integration branch `srvm-phase7`: phases 1-7 complete, lanes running; it lands on master first). Edit ONLY your report `collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md`. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3 (cursor, cursor cell, cursor-ref, cell).\nPhase 8 per `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` section 10 item 8 (\"Cutover\"): delete `yin