{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019ayXWkFJqh9gNDnu3M64FD","type":"tool_result","content":"580\t#### 6.1.4 The C4 corpus, read-only\n581\t\n582\t**PROPOSED.** The linked harness (`test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc`)\n583\tis not edited. A new test namespace defines its own backend map in the\n584\tshape of `h/backends` (`:109-120`) with four entries, `:stack-old`,\n585\t`:stack-new`, `:register-old`, `:register-new`, each building the root\n586\ttask over the program AST with `h/composition` (`:149-158`) and the\n587\tpipeline named, and drives it with `h/drive` (`:161-171`) against\n588\t`h/source` over the harness's published `py` and, for the import\n589\tprograms, the guest modules it publishes itself through\n590\t`h/publish-guest-module!` (`:95-102`), exactly as `import_test.cljc`'s\n591\tprivate `published-guests` does (`:342-363`: the **module packets**\n592\t`k m t w e n`, `import_programs.cljc:176, 11, 225, 276, 334, 378`,\n593\tpublished bottom-up with `t` depending on `k`).\n594\t\n595\t**Two populations, kept apart.**\n596\t\n597\t*(a) Root import programs.* The nine root packets the import tests run,\n598\teach lowered with `lower/lower-packet pk {:prelude :linked}`, with the\n599\texpected outcome the C4 test pins (`import_test.cljc:400-516`), compared\n600\told = new per backend family **and** equal to that pinned outcome:\n601\t\n602\t| Root packet (`import_programs.cljc`) | C4 test | Expected `[halted? blocked? output]` |\n603\t|---|---|---|\n604\t| `o-packet` (`:410`) | `import-orders-statements-test` | `[true false {:py/out [\"a\" \"m-body\" \"b\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n605\t| `q-packet` (`:997`) | `second-import-does-not-re-execute-test` | `[true false {:py/out [\"m-body\" \"done\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n606\t| `d-packet` (`:473`) | same | `[true false {:py/out [\"m-body\" \"7\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n607\t| `c-packet` (`:533`) | `module-dict-mutations-are-shared-test` | `[true false {:py/out [\"m-body\" \"5\" \"absent\" \"('gone', 5)\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n608\t| `r-packet` (`:698`) | `raising-body-removes-its-entry-test` | `[true false {:py/out [\"w-once\" \"cleaned\" \"w-once\" \"again\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n609\t| `x-packet` (`:813`) | `importer-catches-imported-function-exception-test` | `[true false {:py/out [\"caught-e\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n610\t| `nn-packet` (`:1085`) | `one-image-two-names-test` | `[true false {:py/out [\"n\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n611\t| the inline `main` of `one-image-two-names-test` (`import_test.cljc:497-504`: `(require 'py) (require 'pym.n) (py/init!) (py/run-main pym.n/body)`), rebuilt in the test | same | `[true false {:py/out [\"__main__\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n612\t| `s-packet` (`:890`) | `preseeded-modules-resolve-test` | `[true false {:py/out [\"m-body\" \"True\" \"True\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n613\t| `tt-packet` (`:1045`) | `transitive-import-delivers-test` | `[true false {:py/out [\"k-body\" \"t-sees 3\" \"t-done\"] :py/exception nil}]` |\n614\t\n615\tTen root programs, count asserted. Here only the **root program's**\n616\tlowering differs between old and new; the served module bodies (`py`,\n617\tthe six guests) are the publisher's old images until cutover. This\n618\tpopulation therefore covers the new lowering of **root code that links,\n619\timports, catches cross-module exceptions and reads module state**, not\n620\tthe module bodies themselves.\n621\t\n622\t*(b) Module bodies, executed as root programs.* To exercise the new\n623\tlowering of the module code itself without editing C4 files or the\n624\tpublisher, each of the eight module ASTs of §7.3 (`prelude/module-uast`;\n625\tthe `pysp` spec's `:ast`; the six guest specs' `:ast`) is run **as a root\n626\tprogram** on both pipelines under the linked harness: `py`'s own body\n627\trequires nothing and defines its runtime into the store; `pysp`'s body\n628\t`(require 'py)` and defines; a guest's body requires `py` and its\n629\timports and defines. Observable: `[halted? blocked? store]` where `store`\n630\tis the map of what the run left in the task's store, under\n631\t`native-normalize` on the values (closure → `:closure`, else the value),\n632\tcompared old = new. Separately the store's key set is asserted equal to\n633\t`(prelude/defined-keys ast)` (`prelude.cljc:3416-3425`; the module\n634\tfixtures supply top-level placeholders for nested runtime keys, and\n635\t`defined-keys` is a syntactic any-depth scanner, not an execution\n636\toracle). Coverage claimed: top-level execution and closure creation only;\n637\tinvoked module bodies are covered at phase 8.\n638\tThis runs every definition and every top-level expression of every\n639\tmodule body through the new lowering on both kernels.\n640\t\n641\t*(c) Not covered until phase 8.* The install-child path over **newly\n642\tlowered module images** (a `require` that spawns the module's body from\n643\ta manifest whose H/R images came from `derive`) is not exercised by (a)\n644\tor (b), because publishing new images needs the production publisher to\n645\tswitch (§7.6, §8.3). It is covered at phase 8 by the C4 suite itself\n646\t(`import_test`, `linked_prelude_test`, `safepoint_test`), whose pinned\n647\toutcomes then run over new images; §10.4 names that as a phase-8 gate.\n648\t\n649\tObservables for (a) use `render/output` as `import_test`'s `outcome`\n650\tdoes (`:375-378`). `^:slow`, guarded, and it must actually run for\n651\tsign-off (§10 5b item 9).\n652\t\n653\t### 6.2 Validators, liveness, determinism\n654\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14576d0d-3405-4311-bbba-ad13d850656b","uuid":"520242db-134e-49ca-bc2e-2457422ed8c0","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:03:27.699Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8plan/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md","content":"#### 6.1.4 The C4 corpus, read-only\n\n**PROPOSED.** The linked harness (`test/yang/python/antlr/linked_