{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BwqeErMrc9AEdJ4k2w1ARg","type":"tool_result","content":"2072\t### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n2073\t\n2074\t**Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: phases 6 and 7a-7c now provide the entry seams; 7d reports the Stage E port.\n2075\tPhase 7's entry conditions are met: the phase-6 row carrier and frame/layout\n2076\tharness are available; the holder, rows checkpoint inspector, ledger and\n2077\tauthority use packs; free-environment retention is threaded through the\n2078\tlift; recovery format 2 is based on rows. The Stage D composition uses\n2079\tsemantic-register machines and the composition's function `:source-index`\n2080\tseam. The 7d report records the corresponding Stage E world/scenario port\n2081\tand local JVM results; 7d is still in review. Entry readiness is not\n2082\ttri-host phase acceptance: Node/Dart Stage E and the killed four-pair\n2083\tJVM/Node process matrix remain the orchestrator's gates. The owner accepts\n2084\tthe REPL custody gap until phase 8. Versions 0/1/2 remain only as direct\n2085\tlegacy codecs/tests until phase 8, without compatibility or version dispatch\n2086\tin the row holder/authority path. The two backends remain as §4.6 specifies.\n2087\t\n2088\t### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n2089\t\n2090\t| | needs | concurrent with |\n2091\t|---|---|---|\n2092\t| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n2093\t| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n2094\t| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n2095\t| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n2096\t\n2097\tNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n2098\t`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\n2099\tregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\n2100\tnot edited. **Amended after 6c (2026-10-13):** 6c proper held to this:\n2101\tit created `layout.cljc` and `layout_test.cljc`, extended the 6b harness\n2102\tfile and the store-write audit's allowlist, and edited no kernel, no\n2103\t`rows.cljc` and no 4b or phase-5 file. The one further kernel edit this\n2104\tdesign names, the retained-FFI response-pair seam of both de Bruijn\n2105\tkernels (§4.3, 6c-post-D2), is its own slice behind an owner decision\n2106\t(§11, 6c Q2) and is not part of 6c.\n2107\t\n2108\t---\n2109\t\n2110\t## 9. Verification honesty\n2111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14576d0d-3405-4311-bbba-ad13d850656b","uuid":"5d335f6f-950a-4261-9bf0-cea2b74f79b4","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:03:29.422Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8plan/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n\n**Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: phases 6 and 7a-7c now provide the entry seams; 7d reports the Stage E port.\nPhase 7's entry conditions are met: the phase-6 row carrier and frame/layout\nharness are available; the holder, rows checkpoint inspector, ledger and\nauthority use packs; free-environment retention is threaded through the\nlift; recovery format 2 is based on rows. The Stage D composition uses\nsemantic-register machines and the composition's function `:source-index`\nseam. The 7d report records the corresponding Stage E world/scenario port\nand local JVM results; 7d is still in review. Entry readiness is not\ntri-host phase acceptance: Node/Dart Stage E and the killed four-pair\nJVM/Node process matrix remain the orchestrator's gates. The owner accepts\nthe REPL custody gap until phase 8. Versions 0/1/2 remain only as direct\nlegacy codecs/tests until phase 8, without compatibility or version dispatch\nin the row holder/authority path. The two backends remain as §4.6 specifies.\n\n### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n\n| | needs | concurrent with |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n\nNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\nregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\nnot edited. **Amended after 6c (2026-10-13):** 6c proper held to this:\nit created `layout.cljc` and `layout_test.cljc`, extended the 6b harness\nfile and the store-write audit's allowlist, and edited no kernel, no\n`rows.cljc` and no 4b or phase-5 file. The one further kernel edit this\ndesign names, the retained-FFI response-pair seam of both de Bruijn\nkernels (§4.3, 6c-post-D2), is its own slice behind an owner decision\n(§11, 6c Q2) and is not part of 6c.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Verification honesty\n","numLines":40,"startLine":2072,"totalLines":2728}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BwqeErMrc9AEdJ4k2w1ARg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
