{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cg1AhKsK81xxgcFwNNdCM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The report is written to `collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md` in the worktree. Only that file was created; no source or docs were touched.\n\n**Verdict: NOT READY**, blocked on four owner questions.\n\n**What the inventory found that the design did not say:**\n\n- The rename is not drop-in. The old kernel exports `vm-load-program` and `load-image`, which the new one lacks. All 56 requirers of the old namespace need a hand rewrite, 10 of them C4-track Python tests plus the shared linked harness.\n- More de Bruijn code survives than \"delete the lowerers\" suggests. Only resolve, linearize and register-compile die. The code, register-code, register-effects namespaces, both kernels, and the 1641-line projection namespace stay. The projection's SHA-256 node hashes therefore move to BLAKE3.\n- The H descriptor-hash golden has not yet moved to a surviving test. That is a stated precondition of phase 8 and becomes slice 8a's first task.\n- The descriptors change by two rows, not one. The BLAKE3 ruling flips a literal `:hash :sha256` row beside the removed `:dim/lift-to` row, so the derivations document's mechanical check needs a one-line amendment.\n- The old transport has zero production requirers. Its 141 tests and three fixtures can go in one slice. Three new tests borrow helpers from the old support namespaces and must be rewired first.\n- The 7a/7b row fixtures carry A addresses only, no H/R and no format keyword, so they do not regenerate.\n\n**Plan shape:** seven slices, 8ab (descriptors, goldens, BLAKE3 merged so each constant moves once), 8c (production pipeline to A), 8d (old transport out, concurrent), 8e (old lowerers out), 8f (old kernel out, rename in two commits, C4 suite as the install-child gate), 8g (docs). Estimate is 11 to 15 codex days and 14 to 19 review rounds, 4 to 5 weeks calendar.\n\n**Owner questions blocking the first brief:** who edits the 10 C4 files and the two manifest goldens, confirm the old transport dies in 8d, accept the two-row descriptor diff, and the fate of the old `yin.vm.semantic.md` design doc."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":282,"cache_read_input_tokens":205767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":282},"output_tokens":744,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14576d0d-3405-4311-bbba-ad13d850656b","uuid":"089f9cdd-7d34-46a6-af34-a0534162fe69","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:17:28.688Z","request_id":"req_011Cg1AhKbwpDK2jMnWpY3Bn"}
